this makeshift school in bangladesh's  krita palong refugee camp may not look  impressive  but it had offered some 600 rohingya  students a chance to learn and dream of  a better future  now it stands empty after local  authorities forced its closure  [Music]  every human has a dream to become  somebody in life education is very  important for it my ambition is to be a  doctor but alas i cannot even pass the  entrance exam here without proper  education  more than nine hundred thousand rohingya  refugees are living in un established  camps  that's after fleeing a military  crackdown in myanmar in 2017.  since then local groups have attempted  to establish private schools  but it's not the first to be closed for  the past three months schools set up in  camps have been shut down by officials  unicef runs schools for children but  they stop at the age of 14.  school shutdown will create a deep  crisis for the children if they can't go  to school they'll get involved in  something bad  a senior member of the government told a  news agency on condition of anonymity  that it's unacceptable to operate a  school without permission  kfori school principal mohammad shawif  says this is not the case  suddenly armed police in charge of camp  security came in and asked whether we  had written permission from the cap in  charge to operate  we told them we had verbal permission  this school was set up several years ago  by our slain leader master mohib ola who  arranged permission everything ran  smoothly until they raided the school  this week  now there's concern for the students  left languishing in the camps  and many wondering why they're not  receiving the basic right of education  laura about a manly al jazeera
 

